Figure 7: 
Confirmed pl$a$nets as listed by NASA Exoplanet Archive (accessed on 2026 July 3) with host mass measured at better than 50 $\%$. The black symbol with errorbars represents the masses estimate of OGLE-2013-BLG-1125/MOA-2013-BLG-584Lb from this study. The gray dash line indicates the deuterium burning mass limit (defined as 0.013 $M_{\odot}$). The empty star symbols represent the planets of the Solar System Left: Planet mass (or $m_{p}\sin i$ for radial velocity planets) versus host mass. The rectangle highlights five planets discussed in Section 4. Right: Planet mass versus planet semi-major axis. For the majority of planets discovered by microlensing, including OGLE-2013-BLG-1125Lb, the projected separation $a_{\perp}$ (i.e. a lower limit on the true separation a) is plotted. When several entries of the same planets exist, the default is plotted (defined as '1' by the NASA Exoplanet Archive
).
